  "description": "Reid Tract Jr. 20 | 20\" Kids' mountain bike\nBuilt for young adventurers aged 7–9, the Reid Tract Jr. is a 20\" kids' mountain bike designed to help young riders take on everything from neighbourhood rides to exciting off-road trails. With a lightweight alloy frame, front suspension and powerful disc brakes, it's built to give kids the confidence to explore further.\nThe lightweight 6061 alloy frame is designed with increased step-over clearance, making it easier for young riders to get on and off the bike. Aluminium kids' specific components help keep the bike comfortable and manageable for growing riders.\nFront suspension helps absorb bumps and rougher surfaces, with 40mm of travel on the 20\" wheel and 50mm on the 24\" wheel. Alloy rims and wide 2.35\" tyres provide grip and stability across a variety of surfaces, from park paths to local trails.\nThe Shimano 7-speed Tourney gearing gives young riders a useful range of gears for tackling different terrain, while powerful mechanical disc brakes provide reliable stopping and control when things get more adventurous.\nWhether they're riding around the neighbourhood, exploring local parks or heading out on the trails with family, the Tract Jr. gives young riders the freedom to build confidence, develop their skills and enjoy the outdoors.\nWho is the Tract Jr. for?\nThe Tract Jr. 20\" Kids' Mountain Bike is ideal for:\n\nYoung riders aged 7–9\nKids ready to develop their off-road riding skills\nRiders looking for a lightweight alloy mountain bike\nChildren who enjoy exploring parks, trails and outdoor spaces\nYoung cyclists who want the versatility of 7-speed gearing\nRiders who need extra control on bumps and varied terrain\nKids who want to ride alongside parents and older riders\nEveryday adventures, family rides and weekend trail trips\n\nFind the right fit\nChoosing the right bike size helps young riders ride comfortably, confidently and safely. The Tract Jr. is designed for riders aged 7–9, with 20\" and 24\" wheel options available depending on the rider's size. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right bike based on your child's height and age.",
